{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2126 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "3758158d0cef6e11fd641db3f8fc58ebc540b96a2f146112d938a83973b85adb" :edb/db-before-t 2125 :edb/db-after-t 2126 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535438 50 #inst "2026-10-09T00:04:52.228Z" 13194139535438 true] [17592186171799 1100 "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface defined by the equations\n$x=u, \\quad y=1+u^2, \\quad z=v^2$\nat the point where $u=1$ and $v=2$." 13194139535438 false] [17592186171799 1100 "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=u, \\quad \ny=1+u^2, \\quad\nz=v^2\n$$\n\nat the point where $u=1$ and $v=2.$" 13194139535438 true] [17592186171799 1145 "In vector form, our surface has the equation\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\big\\langle u, \\: 1 + u^2, \\: v^2\\big\\rangle\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′}(u, v) &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u}, \\frac{∂y}{∂u}, \\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(1 + u^{2}), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(v^{2})⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨1, 2u, 0⟩ \\\\\nr_{v}^{′}(u, v) &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v}, \\frac{∂y}{∂v}, \\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(1 + u^{2}), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(v^{2})⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨0, 0, 2v⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=2{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′}(1, 2) &= ⟨1, 2(1), 0⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨1, 2, 0⟩ \\\\\nr_{v}^{′}(1, 2) &= ⟨0, 0, 2(2)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨0, 0, 4⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point where $u=1$ and $v=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nn &= r_{u}^{′}(1, 2) \\cdot r_{v}^{′}(1, 2) \\\\\n&=\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= ⟨\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix}, -\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix},\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨8,-4, 0⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535438 false] [17592186171799 1145 "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\big\\langle u, \\: 1 + u^2, \\: v^2\\big\\rangle.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1+{u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2u,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1+{u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,2v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=2{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,2) & =⟨1,\\,2(1),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,2) & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,2(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point where $u=1$ and $v=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,2)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,2) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,\\,-4,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535438 true] [17592186171800 1100 "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface generated by the vector-valued function ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/assets/e81d44c7891de67ac97b59abe1bd1c2b67335bb809e3dc5031a6c21b33785eda.png) at the point ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/assets/2a1d8507dddd64183827d51345a244628443cf3ed30f86249131ccb8c1e855ee.png)" 13194139535438 true] [17592186171800 1100 "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface generated by the vector-valued function $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)= \\big\\langle u^2-2, \\: u-v, \\: v^3+1 \\big\\rangle$ at the point $(-1,2,0)$." 13194139535438 false] [17592186171800 1145 "First, notice that since ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/assets/a7bc8338d348d8e1c18ac970870593c29560ff3c349e31796b62dcd1c35cfcd1.png) lies on the surface, we obtain\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/assets/d62dba719e321fcd67f78f9ec20b2cffe5fb5ed00d4a2c65392e1520632a1e38.png)\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/assets/5a87223bfdfcf175ccbdd1f94ebd06d92ab9ad841cbb9cf59dab31940fa61c40.png)\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/assets/0d1b1e8a3ef8680d59a924e596e06a0cdccc946ee2cc426527f2de7893f69564.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/assets/00341d0f3526e0407ed756cb16b940e213fb30f762e55370e13006ac8f603f37.png)\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/assets/f4c33acdfdc112d5e252f26cfd33a172fff21f412adbb0071ebcb50f561deaa8.png)\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/assets/c4a233bd69566c25e0aeb6736d21dca4aff73a92015a2831d0d0e8fb0243f7ec.png) is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/assets/722fa4913d73cae67f202a7a25fec74cdad63866bb4297bf8e8058b4808f4c20.png)" 13194139535438 true] [17592186171800 1145 "First, notice that since $(-1,2,0)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{u^{2} - 2 =-1; u - v = 2; v^{3} + 1 = 0\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′}(u, v) &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u}, \\frac{∂y}{∂u}, \\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u^{2} - 2), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(u - v), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(v^{3} + 1)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨2u, 1, 0⟩ \\\\\nr_{v}^{′}(u, v) &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v}, \\frac{∂y}{∂v}, \\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u^{2} - 2), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(u - v), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(v^{3} + 1)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨0,-1, 3v^{2}⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=-1{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′}(1,-1) &= ⟨2(1), 1, 0⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨2, 1, 0⟩ \\\\\nr_{v}^{′}(1,-1) &= ⟨0,-1, 3(-1)^{2}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨0,-1, 3⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point $(3,1,0)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nn &= r_{u}^{′}(1,-1) \\cdot r_{v}^{′}(1,-1) \\\\\n&=\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= ⟨\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{vmatrix}, -\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix},\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨3,-6,-2⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535438 false] [17592186171801 1100 "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface generated by the vector-valued function $\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\big\\langle v^2, \\: u-v, \\: u^2 \\big\\rangle$ at the point where $u=2$ and $v=-1$." 13194139535438 false] [17592186171801 1100 "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface generated by the vector-valued function $\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\big\\langle v^2, \\: u-v, \\: u^2 \\big\\rangle$ at the point where $u=2$ and $v=-1.$" 13194139535438 true] [17592186171801 1145 "We first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′}(u, v) &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u}, \\frac{∂y}{∂u}, \\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v^{2}), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(u - v), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(u^{2})⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨0, 1, 2u⟩ \\\\\nr_{v}^{′}(u, v) &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v}, \\frac{∂y}{∂v}, \\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v^{2}), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(u - v), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(u^{2})⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨2v,-1, 0⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these vectors when $u=2$ and $v=-1{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′}(2,-1) &= ⟨0, 1, 2(2)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨0, 1, 4⟩ \\\\\nr_{v}^{′}(2,-1) &= ⟨2(-1),-1, 0⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 2,-1, 0⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nn &= r_{u}^{′}(2,-1) \\cdot r_{v}^{′}(2,-1) \\\\\n&=\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= ⟨\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}, -\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{vmatrix},\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨4,-8, 2⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the parameters $u=2$ and $v=-1$ correspond to the point\n\n$$\n\\big((-1)^2, \\: 2-(-1), \\: 2^2 \\big) = (1, 3, 4)\n$$\n\nthe equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nn \\cdot ⟨x - x_{0}, y - y_{0}, z - z_{0}⟩ &= 0 \\\\\n⟨4,-8, 2⟩ \\cdot ⟨x - 1, y - 3, z - 4⟩ &= 0 \\\\\n4 \\cdot (x - 1) + (-8) \\cdot (y - 3) + 2 \\cdot (z - 4) &= 0 \\\\\n4x - 8y + 2z + 12 &= 0 \\\\\n2x - 4y + z + 6 &= 0 \\\\\n2x - 4y + z &= -6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535438 false] [17592186171801 1145 "We first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2v,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these vectors when $u=2$ and $v=-1{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(2,-1) & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,4⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(2,-1) & =⟨2(-1),\\,-1,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(2,-1)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(2,-1) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,-8,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the parameters $u=2$ and $v=-1$ correspond to the point \n\n$$\n\\big( (-1)^2, \\: 2-(-1), \\: 2^2 \\big) = (1, 3, 4),\n$$\n\nthe equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨4,\\,-8,\\,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-3,\\,z-4⟩ & =0 \\\\ 4\\cdot (x-1)+(-8)\\cdot (y-3)+2\\cdot (z-4) & =0 \\\\ 4x-8y+2z+12 & =0 \\\\ 2x-4y+z+6 & =0 \\\\ 2x-4y+z & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535438 true] [17592186171802 1100 "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx=u+v, \\quad\ny=3u^2, \\quad\nz=u-v\n$$\n\nat the point $(2 ,3, 0).$" 13194139535438 true] [17592186171802 1100 "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface defined by the equations\n$x=u+v, \\quad y=3u^2, \\quad z=u-v$\nat the point $(2,3, 0)$." 13194139535438 false] [17592186171802 1145 "In vector form, our surface has the equation\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\big\\langle u+v, \\: 3u^2, \\: u-v \\big\\rangle\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since $(2, 3, 0)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{u + v = 2; 3u^{2} = 3; u - v = 0\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′}(u, v) &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u}, \\frac{∂y}{∂u}, \\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u + v), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(3u^{2}), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(u - v)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨1, 6u, 1⟩ \\\\\nr_{v}^{′}(u, v) &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v}, \\frac{∂y}{∂v}, \\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u + v), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(3u^{2}), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(u - v)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨1, 0,-1⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=1{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′}(1, 1) &= ⟨1, 6(1), 1⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨1, 6, 1⟩ \\\\\nr_{v}^{′}(1, 1) &= ⟨1, 0,-1⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nn &= r_{u}^{′}(1, 1) \\cdot r_{v}^{′}(1, 1) \\\\\n&=\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= ⟨\\begin{vmatrix}6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix}, -\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix},\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 6, 2,-6⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nn \\cdot ⟨x - x_{0}, y - y_{0}, z - z_{0}⟩ &= 0 \\\\\n⟨ - 6, 2,-6⟩ \\cdot ⟨x - 2, y - 3, z⟩ &= 0 \\\\\n(-6) \\cdot (x - 2) + 2 \\cdot (y - 3) + (-6) \\cdot z &= 0 \\\\\n- 6x + 2y - 6z + 6 &= 0 \\\\\n- 3x + y - 3z + 3 &= 0 \\\\\n3x - y + 3z &= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535438 false] [17592186171802 1145 "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\big\\langle u+v, \\: 3u^2, \\: u-v \\big\\rangle.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since $(2, 3, 0)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064857/assets/9a57281535511312d2fda6f388161fcd624354785d73d48954d10f9e7821653b.png)\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3{u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,6u,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3{u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=1{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,1) & =⟨1,\\,6(1),\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,6,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,1) & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,1)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,1) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6,\\,2,\\,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-6,\\,2,\\,-6⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-3,\\,z⟩ & =0 \\\\ (-6)\\cdot (x-2)+2\\cdot (y-3)+(-6)\\cdot z & =0 \\\\ -6x+2y-6z+6 & =0 \\\\ -3x+y-3z+3 & =0 \\\\ 3x-y+3z & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535438 true] [17592186171993 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349212 13194139535438 true] [17592186171993 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349219 13194139535438 true] [17592186171993 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349226 13194139535438 true] [17592186171994 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349233 13194139535438 true] [17592186171994 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349240 13194139535438 true] [17592186171994 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349247 13194139535438 true] [17592186171994 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349254 13194139535438 true] [17592186171994 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349261 13194139535438 true] [17592186171995 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349156 13194139535438 true] [17592186171995 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349163 13194139535438 true] [17592186171995 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349170 13194139535438 true] [17592186171995 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349177 13194139535438 true] [17592186171996 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349184 13194139535438 true] [17592186171996 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349191 13194139535438 true] [17592186171996 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349198 13194139535438 true] [17592186171996 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349205 13194139535438 true] [17592186172154 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535438 true] [17592186172154 1100 "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface defined by the equations\n\n$x = u + v, y = u^{2}v, z = v$\nat the point where $u = 1$ and $v = 2$." 13194139535438 false] [17592186172154 1100 "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=u+v,\\,y={u}^{2}v,\\,z=v\n$$\n\nat the point where $u=1$ and $v=2.$" 13194139535438 true] [17592186172154 1145 "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,{u}^{2}v,\\,v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2uv,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,{u}^{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,2) & =⟨1,\\,2(1)(2),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,4,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,2) & =⟨1,\\,(1)^{2},\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point where $u=1$ and $v=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,2)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,2) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,-1,\\,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535438 true] [17592186172156 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535438 true] [17592186172156 1100 "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u, v) = ⟨2u, u\\sin v, 4u^{2}⟩$ at the point where $u = 1$ and $v = π$." 13194139535438 false] [17592186172156 1100 "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨2u,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,4{u}^{2}⟩$ at the point where $u=1$ and $v=\\pi .$" 13194139535438 true] [17592186172156 1145 "We first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(4{u}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,8u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(4{u}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these vectors when $u=1$ and $v=\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,\\pi ) & =⟨2,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ),\\,8(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,0,\\,8⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,\\pi ) & =⟨0,\\,(1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,\\pi )\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,\\pi ) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,\\,0,\\,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the parameters $u=1$ and $v=\\pi $ correspond to the point \n\n$$\n(2(1),\\,(1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ),\\,4(1)^{2})=(2,0,4),\n$$\n\nthe equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨8,\\,0,\\,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y,\\,z-4⟩ & =0 \\\\ 8\\cdot (x-2)+0\\cdot y+(-2)\\cdot (z-4) & =0 \\\\ 8x-2z-8 & =0 \\\\ 4x-z & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535438 true] [17592186172190 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535438 true] [17592186172190 1100 "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx={u}^{2},\\,y={v}^{2},\\,z=u+2v\n$$\n\nat the point $(4,1,4).$" 13194139535438 true] [17592186172190 1100 "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface defined by the equations\n\n$x = u^{2}, y = v^{2}, z = u + 2v$\nat the point $(4, 1, 4)$." 13194139535438 false] [17592186172190 1145 "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,u+2v⟩.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since $(4,1,4)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}=4 \\\\ {v}^{2}=1 \\\\ u+2v=4\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=2 \\\\ v=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2v,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=2$ and $v=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(2,1) & =⟨2(2),\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(2,1) & =⟨0,\\,2(1),\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(2,1)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(2,1) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,-8,\\,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-2,\\,-8,\\,8⟩\\cdot ⟨x-4,\\,y-1,\\,z-4⟩ & =0 \\\\ (-2)\\cdot (x-4)+(-8)\\cdot (y-1)+8\\cdot (z-4) & =0 \\\\ -2x-8y+8z-16 & =0 \\\\ -x-4y+4z-8 & =0 \\\\ x+4y-4z & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535438 true] [17592186172191 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535438 true] [17592186172191 1100 "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface defined by the equations\n\n$x = u\\cos v, y = u, z = u\\sin v$\nat the point where $u = 1$ and $v = \\frac{π}{2}$." 13194139535438 false] [17592186172191 1100 "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,y=u,\\,z=u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nat the point where $u=1$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" 13194139535438 true] [17592186172191 1145 "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,1,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,0,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,1,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨-1\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0,\\,1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,0,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point where $u=1$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535438 true] [17592186349156 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349157 13194139535438 true] [17592186349156 1089 "q-109707" 13194139535438 true] [17592186349156 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535438 true] [17592186349156 1100 "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,u+v,\\,uv⟩$ at the point where $u=1$ and $v=1.$" 13194139535438 true] [17592186349156 1113 #uuid "2edd9c1d-c147-5e5b-9fc6-73e22654b300" 13194139535438 true] [17592186349156 1145 "We first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}-{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,1,\\,v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}-{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2v,\\,1,\\,u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these vectors when $u=1$ and $v=1$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,1) & =⟨2(1),\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,1) & =⟨-2(1),\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,1)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,1) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-4,\\,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the parameters $u=1$ and $v=1$ correspond to the point \n\n$$\n({1}^{2}-{1}^{2},\\,1+1,\\,1\\cdot 1)=(0,2,1),\n$$\n\nthe equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨0,\\,-4,\\,4⟩\\cdot ⟨x,\\,y-2,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 0\\cdot x+(-4)\\cdot (y-2)+4\\cdot (z-1) & =0 \\\\ -4y+4z+4 & =0 \\\\ -y+z+1 & =0 \\\\ y-z & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535438 true] [17592186349157 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349158 13194139535438 