-bd01-5a1d-b671-65013c352e27" 13194139535438 true] [17592186349163 1145 "We first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2{u}^{3}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2{u}^{3}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2uv,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these vectors when $u=1$ and $v=3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,3) & =⟨6(1)^{2},\\,{3}^{2},\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,\\,9,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,3) & =⟨0,\\,2(1)(3),\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,6,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,3)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,3) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 6 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨18,\\,-12,\\,36⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the parameters $u=1$ and $v=3$ correspond to the point \n\n$$\n(2(1)^{3},\\,1(3)^{2},\\,2(3))=(2,9,6),\n$$\n\nthe equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨18,\\,-12,\\,36⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-9,\\,z-6⟩ & =0 \\\\ 18\\cdot (x-2)-12\\cdot (y-9)+36\\cdot (z-6) & =0 \\\\ 18x-12y+36z-144 & =0 \\\\ 3x-2y+6z-24 & =0 \\\\ 3x-2y+6z & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535438 true] [17592186349164 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349165 13194139535438 true] [17592186349164 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349166 13194139535438 true] [17592186349164 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349167 13194139535438 true] [17592186349164 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349168 13194139535438 true] [17592186349164 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349169 13194139535438 true] [17592186349164 1040 #edb/re